# Security and Privacy Rules

- Treat all identity fields as sensitive even though repository data is synthetic.
- Minimize sensitive data in logs, exceptions, fixtures, and generated evidence.
- Reject unsafe path traversal and malformed identifiers.
- Preserve correlation IDs without exposing raw identity content.
- Any new persistence, telemetry, provider integration, or reviewer flow requires an explicit security/privacy spec update.
- Security controls require executable tests or review evidence; prose-only claims are insufficient.
